  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building justice and peace through PEACE &amp; JUSTICE in Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PEACE &amp; JUSTICE will strengthen the coping mechanism of youth aged 12-35 (70% refugees and 30% host community population) in Kiryandongo refugee settlement through provision of psychosocial support and trainings in policy advocacy. Using the acquired knowledge &amp; skills, youth will participate in the formulation and implementation of policies at district and national levels. Emphasis will be put on policies such as National Action Plan on UNSCR 1325 which recognise impacts of conflict on women.</narrative>
  </description>
